WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.020
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:08.650
I see.  You destroyed Cyberse World.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.320
I'll ready our real 
battlefield somewhere else.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.760
We declare war on you.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.070
That time will come.  Let's go.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:29.270
Ai, similar to how you're modeled after 
Playmaker, I was required to be modeled after someone.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.510
You two.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.750
If Lightning is your creator, 
then model yourself after him!

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:43.260
He's aware of his own superiority, 
but he knows that he's not perfect.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.260
He believes that if the Ignis remain as is...

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:52.920
...the Ignis will foolishly and fruitlessly 
battle each other, like humans.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.070
Lightning wanted to unify the Ignis 
into one before that happened.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.660
I'm the vessel who'll unite 
the Ignis to evolve them.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.120
Among creatures, humans have evolved well.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.800
But you passed your peak.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:16.050
The speed of human evolution 
is slower than ours.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.380
Well, Playmaker?

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.880
Can humans defeat AI?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.060
Let's duel.  Winner gets me and Ai.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.100
If you win, you'll prove human's superiority.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.370
And I'll disappear, and Lightning's 
plans can be stopped.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.960
Bring it on, Bohman!  Speed Duel!

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:00.350
Our lives aren't forever

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:07.140
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:14.460
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:21.040
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:27.780
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:35.010
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:41.720
I want to share your pain

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:14.610
Playmaker and Soulburner have split apart.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:18.480
Don't let them get away, Yusaku and Takeru!

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:26.960
Before we begin our duel, let's compete to 
see who goes first or second, Playmaker.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.170
Whoa!  No way!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.770
You're going first!

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.190
We know your deck's better 
when you go second!

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:41.340
I see.  As much as I'd like to agree, 
that won't be true competition.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.280
Follow me, Playmaker.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.810
He fled!  After him, Playmaker!

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:49.770
I know!

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:01.550
We just passed through this Cyberse World.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.460
The Ignis tower!

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.250
Don't lose your cool.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.210
This world is fake.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:15.970
I know!

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.440
I know... but...

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:25.110
After I left, this happened 
to my homeworld...

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.550
No, it was actually much worse.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:36.290
I know because I destroyed 
Cyberse World with my own hands.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.290
Into dust.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.260
Completely!  Without mercy!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.000
You!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:50.260
I remember the Cyberses' 
cries as they burned!

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.900
I won't forgive you...

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.950
I won't forgive you, Bohman!

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.200
Don't let him provoke you, Ai.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.220
He's trying to make us lose our cool.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.150
The competition has already started.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.120
I know!

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:12.860
But...  Is he the type of guy who'd do this?

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.300
Well, Playmaker?

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:20.430
Like he said, he may have evolved quickly.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:27.750
Playmaker, how about whoever passes the tower 
first gets to choose who goes first and second?

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.040
Fine!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.210
Let's do it!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.690
He's that good at riding his board?

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.830
Be careful, Playmaker!

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:53.180
A strong Data Storm blows around the tower.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.290
If you get caught, it's over!

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.270
Seems so.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:01.440
It's like the time we fought 
Revolver at the Tower of Hanoi.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:05.740
Back then, I didn't think the 
Ignis would fight each other.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:10.450
But it seems I fought for this to happen now.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.980
If you don't like it, we 
have to change the future.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:18.050
But will the future really change?

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:21.050
The future doesn't change.  
You change the future!

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.810
By defeating Bohman!

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.700
Playmaker...

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.630
Right!  Let's beat him together!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.580
Playmaker!

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.480
Yusaku!

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.420
He's okay.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.920
I'm counting on you, Yusaku!

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.050
I won.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:03.230
I choose to go second.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.260
You punk!

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.230
Let's go, Playmaker!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.130
Speed Duel!

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.810
My turn!

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.420
What'll you do, Playmaker?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:20.770
If he uses Judgment Arrows, it'll 
double his Link Monsters' ATK.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:25.020
If you end your turn carelessly, 
he'll crush you instantly!

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.420
You're right.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.630
I'll create a formation to 
survive his attack this turn.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.170
I activate the spell card, Cynet Mining!

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:40.940
I discard a card to add a Level 4 or 
lower Cyberse from my deck to my hand.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:47.190
I send Dotscaper to the graveyard 
to add Cyberse Gadget to my hand.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.020
Then I summon Cyberse Gadget!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.650
Cyberse Gadget's effect activates!

00:07:56.650 --> 00:08:00.630
When it's summoned, I Special 
Summon a Level 2 or lower monster

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.630
from my graveyard in defense position.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:05.280
Resurrect, Dotscaper!

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.220
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:13.810
The summoning condition 
is one Level 1 monster!

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.270
Link Summon!

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.670
Link 1 Linkuriboh!

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:22.280
Dotscaper's effect now 
activates from the graveyard!

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:26.850
When it's sent to the graveyard, 
it Special Summons itself!

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.460
Resurrect, Dotscaper!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:34.560
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.330
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:41.970
I set Cyberse Gadget and 
Linkuriboh in the Link Markers!

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.240
Link Summon!

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:49.010
Appear, Link 2 Cyberse Witch!

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.440
Cyberse Gadget's effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:58.180
When it's sent from the field to the 
graveyard, I Special Summon a Gadget Token.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:02.420
Next, Cyberse Witch's effect!

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.610
When a monster is Special 
Summoned next to its link,

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:07.900
I banish a spell card from my graveyard.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:12.900
I add a Cyberse Ritual Monster and 
Ritual Spell from my deck to my hand.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:15.900
I banish Cynet Mining!

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:20.840
I add Cyberse Magician and 
Cynet Ritual to my hand!

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.310
Then Cyberse Witch's effect!

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:27.320
I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower Cyberse from my graveyard!

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.210
Resurrect, Cyberse Gadget!

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:35.520
I activate the Ritual Spell, Cynet Ritual!

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:43.800
I tribute Level 2 Gadget Token, Level 
4 Cyberse Gadget and Level 1 Dotscaper!

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.330
Ritual Summon!

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:50.280
Descend, Cyberse Magician!

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:57.310
I equip the Equip Spell, Grid 
Rod on Cyberse Magician!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:02.780
The equipped monster gains 300 ATK, and 
it's not affected by your card effects.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.960
And once per turn, battle 
or effects can't destroy it!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.460
All right!  Perfect, Playmaker!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.930
I end my turn.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:17.660
I see.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:23.100
On his first turn, he was able to get 
Cyberse Magician to halve damage.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.540
He strengthened his defenses.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.100
Cyberse Magician has 2800 ATK.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:33.140
You're using him and Grid 
Rod to stop my attacks.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.140
But will it be enough to survive my attacks?

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:40.420
Witness how I evolved!

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:42.890
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.360
I summon Hydradrive Booster.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.030
Appear!  The circuit that connects the truth!

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.130
Link Summon!

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.740
Link 1 Flow Hydradrive!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:02.340
I activate the spell 
card, Hydradrive Rebuild!

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.970
I destroy one Hydradrive on my field.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.810
I destroy Flow Hydradrive!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.950
He destroyed his own Flow Hydradrive?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:17.790
When Flow Hydradrive is destroyed, 
it Special Summons a Token.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:23.660
I Special Summon a Hydradrive 
Token in defense position!

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.150
But why a Token?

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:29.090
Next, Hydradrive Rebuild's effect.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:34.280
When a Hydradrive destroyed by this card 
activates its effect from the graveyard...

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:38.440
...I Special Summon a Hydradrive from 
the graveyard by negating its effects.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:42.310
Resurrect, Flow Hydradrive!

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.860
I see.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:50.890
You destroyed your own Flow Hydradrive to 
move your Link Monster to the Main Monster Zone.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.370
Exactly, Playmaker.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:57.770
I activate the Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:01.950
Appear!  The three arrows 
that judge the world!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.870
There's his Link Spell!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.840
It doubles a linked monster's ATK!

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:12.180
I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, Hydradrive Defragment!

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:17.140
When an effect destroys my 
Hydradrive Link Monster...

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:20.420
...I destroy one of your spell 
and trap cards this turn.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.920
I destroy Grid Rod!

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:34.270
But even if you double Flow Hydradrive's 
ATK, Cyberse Magician will still have more ATK!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.740
That is true.

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:40.000
But the way I am now, it's 
not enough to stop me!

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:43.470
Appear!  The circuit that connects the truth!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:47.400
The summoning condition is one Hydradrive!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:52.520
Link Summon!  Link 1 Burn Hydradrive!

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:57.130
Hydradrive Defragment's effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:02.700
By banishing it, I add a Hydradrive 
spell card in the graveyard to my hand.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:07.090
I add Hydradrive Rebuild to my hand!

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:11.110
He got back the card that 
destroys his own monster.

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.070
That means...!

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.340
I activate the spell card, 
Hydradrive Rebuild again!

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.310
I destroy Burn Hydradrive!

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.920
Burn Hydradrive's effect activates!

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:28.270
I Special Summon a Hydradrive 
Token in defense position.

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:31.020
Then Hydradrive Rebuild's effect!

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:34.090
Burn Hydradrive resurrects!

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:38.830
Appear!  The circuit that connects the truth!

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:42.200
The summoning condition is one Hydradrive!

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:43.940
Link Summon!

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:46.940
Link 1 Coolant Hydradrive!

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:50.070
He now has three Link 1s.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.690
A Link 3 is coming!

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:56.500
Appear!  The circuit that connects the truth!

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.590
The summoning conditions are 
three Hydradrive Link Monsters!

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.320
Link Summon!

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.160
Come out, the cursed conqueror!

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:09.780
Link 3 Trident Hydradrive Lord!

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:13.980
A Link 3 Hydradrive has arrived!

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:23.750
Trident Hydradrive Lord's effect activates!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:28.970
When it's Link Summoned, it gains the 
Attributes of the three Hydradrives used to summon it.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.720
And your monsters with those Attributes 
have their effects negated!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:38.970
That monster's Attributes 
are Wind, Water and Fire.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:42.490
But Cyberse Magician is Dark Attribute!

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:44.430
Its effects won't be negated!

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:50.670
But if I use Judgment Arrows's effect, 
it will have more ATK than yours.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.550
This is bad!

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:56.380
I set one card!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.280
Go, Trident Hydradrive Lord!

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:03.410
Attack Cyberse Magician!

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.750
Then Judgment Arrows's effect!

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:10.090
Trident Hydradrive Lord's ATK are doubled!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.390
Cyberse Magician's effect!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:20.230
When it battles a Link 
Monster, it gains 1000 ATK!

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:24.470
That amount of ATK is futile.

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:28.570
From my graveyard, the Equip 
Spell, Grid Rod's effect!

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.580
On the turn it's sent to the graveyard...

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:36.050
...the formerly equipped monster can't 
be destroyed in battle or by effects!

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:41.920
And Cyberse Magician 
halves the damage I take!

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.520
Cyberse Architect!

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:54.000
I end my turn.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.000
You managed to survive this turn.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.580
But can you survive my next attack?

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:04.680
Damn!  But I won't lose until 
I get revenge for my homeworld!

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:06.560
Go, Playmaker!

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.950
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.550
That card is...

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:17.190
I equip the Equip Spell, Resume 
Mace on Cyberse Magician!

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:27.320
The equipped monster loses 800 ATK!

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.570
He lowered his own ATK?

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:38.540
But by sending this card to the graveyard, 
the monster's original ATK are doubled!

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:39.980
I see.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:44.020
That's how you'll destroy 
my Trident Hydradrive Lord.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.880
Here I go, Bohman!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.260
Wait, Playmaker!

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:50.990
We have one more card in our hand.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.490
Use it!

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:54.550
One more card?

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:58.800
The Equip Spell, Suspend Wand.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:02.400
Playmaker!  End it now!

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:05.400
I hate to admit it, but 
he's much stronger now.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.540
A chance to defeat him 
won't come around easily!

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.320
What's wrong, Ai?

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:14.900
Something inside me says he 
has to be defeated right now!

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:16.550
What's inside you?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.140
I don't know.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:24.140
But I sometimes feel it during a duel.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.440
Please, Playmaker!

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.500
Fine, Ai.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:36.200
I equip the Equip Spell, Suspend 
Wand on Cyberse Magician!

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.780
A new Equip Spell?

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.200
Go, Cyberse Magician!

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:50.190
Attack Trident Hydradrive Lord!

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.180
Now Suspend Wand's effect!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:58.790
You're using the new Equip Spell's 
effect instead of Resume Mace?

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:04.110
When the equipped monster attacks, 
it can't be destroyed in battle!

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:07.330
And the damage I take is doubled!

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:08.570
What?

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:10.800
Judgment Arrows's effect!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:15.310
Trident Hydradrive Lord's ATK are doubled!

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.810
Cyberse Magician's effect!

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:21.190
Cyberse Magician gains 1000 ATK!

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.640
No way!

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.380
He doubled his own damage?

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:36.230
1900 x 2 is 3800.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:40.090
If this gets through, 
Playmaker will be out of LP!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:45.460
But when Cyberse Magician is 
on the field, damage is halved.

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:50.680
So Playmaker takes 1900 damage, 
which is neither less or more!

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:54.320
Suspend Wand's effect!

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.920
The equipped monster can attack again!

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:59.920
Multiple attacks?

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:02.560
Go, Cyberse Magician!

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.790
Attack Trident Hydradrive Lord again!

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:09.290
The Equip Spell, Resume Mace's effect!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.790
When the equipped monster attacks 
a monster with higher ATK...

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:19.750
...by sending this card to the graveyard, 
the monster's original ATK are doubled!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.010
Judgment Arrows's effect!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.890
My ATK double!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.280
Cyberse Magician's effect!

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:32.280
It gains 1000 ATK!

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:36.590
Then Suspend Wand's effect!

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:39.090
By sending it to the graveyard...

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:46.420
...Cyberse Magician gains ATK equal to 
the damage I took in battle this turn!

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:49.270
7900 ATK!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.390
He was going for this combo.

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:57.740
He could have destroyed Trident Hydradrive 
Lord using just Resume Mace's effect.

00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:02.690
But instead, Playmaker's going for broke.

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:03.980
Why?

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.450
Why, Playmaker?

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:16.630
I see.  It was your suggestion, Ai.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:19.030
Go, Cyberse Magician!

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:22.530
Cyberse Magic!

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.490
This is bad!

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:35.510
Playmaker can still attack 
with Cyberse Witch!

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:37.750
If he takes that attack...

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:40.480
Finish him, Playmaker!

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:42.740
Defeat him this turn!

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:44.480
Go!

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:48.450
Sorry, but I can't let 
that attack get through.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:51.580
The Continuous Trap, Property Flash!

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:57.840
For every 1000 battle damage I took, I 
place a Property Counter on this card.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:02.270
And then the battle ends!

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:03.360
What?

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.650
That means you can't end him!

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:09.920
That attack was unlike you, Playmaker.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:13.320
You were misled by the Dark Ignis.

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:17.250
Why are you so impatient, Ai?

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:20.480
I'm not impatient!

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:25.730
It's just that a voice inside me 
said you needed to be defeated!

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:28.180
A voice inside you?

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:33.740
I see.  Now I understand 
what Lightning was saying.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:37.080
What you have and I don't...

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:40.950
It led you to dig your own grave.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.440
What only I have?

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.680
That's right.

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:49.650
What you have is instinct, Ai!

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:51.110
What?

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.660
Instinct?

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:59.750
As Lightning said, you may 
truly be a special AI.

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:23.870
Trapped in conventionality

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.310
Even denials are obvious

00:22:25.310 --> 00:22:26.440
That There This Whichever

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:28.280
Hey, isn't it true?

00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:29.940
Why is it before you wake up

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:31.510
You build a wall, saying it's impossible

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:32.680
No discussions, no ideals

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:39.720
Even together, it's not the same

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:42.790
Break yourself through  go way

00:22:42.990 --> 00:22:45.930
Even if you lose your 
way, keep moving forward

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.000
Our desires won't be stopped

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:57.570
Let your emotions spill

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:03.710
Keep rewriting  only glory

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:09.120
If we're together

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:12.520
We can seize it

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:39.150
Ai's bad feeling was correct.

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:45.800
The awakened Bohman uses Storm Access 
to acquire the monster that suits him.

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:53.780
But just when defeat was inevitable, a 
new light resides in Playmaker's hand!

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:55.650
I activate my Skill!

00:23:55.650 --> 00:23:58.030
Neo Storm Access!

00:23:58.030 --> 00:24:02.240
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Light Blade that Slices Despair

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:04.360
Into the VRAINS!
